  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive Education for Children on the Move in Emergency Situations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jointly with the Ministry of Education of Ecuador and the Education Workgroup of the GTRM (R4V) platform, the Multi Year Programme has been designed in order to promote access to education for migrant and refugee populations from Venezuela in Ecuador. This Multi Year Programme gives continuity to the First Emergency Response (FER) programme, financed by Education Cannot Wait (ECW) during 2019 and 2020. In the FER UNESCO acted as a Subgrantee.
The overarching goal of the ECW Multi-Year Resilience Programme (MYRP) for Ecuador is to ensure continued access to inclusive and equitable quality education for approximately 105,000 refugee, migrant and host community children and youth.</narrative>
  </description>
